cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "AlphaCurvature: a Lean 4 proof of the Gibilisco–Isola conjecture on the scalar curvature of the α-geometries"
authors:
  - family-names: Bornemann
    given-names: Adam
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
  - name: "Claude (Anthropic)"
license: Apache-2.0
# doi: (add the Zenodo DOI after the first release)
# repository-code: (add the repository URL)
type: software
abstract: >-
  A formal proof, in Lean 4 with Mathlib, of Conjecture 4.1 of P. Gibilisco and
  T. Isola (J. Math. Phys. 46 (2005)), restated as open in P. Gibilisco, Entropy
  22 (2020) 1409: on the open probability simplex with at least three points, the
  scalar curvature of the α-geometry, the pullback of the Euclidean metric by the
  Amari embedding ρ ↦ p ρ^(1/p), is strictly Schur-increasing for p in (2, ∞] and
  strictly Schur-decreasing for p in (1, 2). The proof formalizes a closed form of
  the scalar curvature in power sums, applies the Schur–Ostrowski criterion, and
  shows that the gradient numerator splits into one explicit term per point, each
  of which has the required sign. The endpoint p = ∞ was formalized earlier in
  the trureturing project (github.com/the-omega-institute/trureturing, pull
  request 15566).
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
  - information geometry
  - α-geometry
  - Amari embedding
  - scalar curvature
  - majorization
  - Schur-convexity
